{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And one he-goat for a sin-offering to HaShem.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'for HaShem,' as in (Leviticus 16:8) ״עליו הגורל לה' ועשהו חטאת״ — 'the lot fell upon it for HaShem,' and you make it a sin-offering. Or one may say: חטאת לה' — for the sin that a person commits against HaShem, for thus the language of חטאת in the sacred tongue when it comes with the letter lamed attaches the sin only to the person who sins, as in (Genesis 39:9) ״וחטאתי לאלהים״, (Genesis 44:32) ״וחטאתי לאבי״. But according to what the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded, it is the reverse, and the matter belongs to the secrets of the Torah." "<b>And by way of the Midrash</b> — לחטאת לה' (a sin-offering to HaShem): a sin that none recognizes but HaShem. Thus they expounded in tractate Shevu'ot, for the he-goat of the new moon atones for one who entered the Sanctuary in impurity unwittingly, without any knowledge at all. And they further expounded: Reish Lakish said — what is different about the he-goat of Rosh Chodesh, that it is written of it חטאת לה'? The Holy One, blessed be He, said: this he-goat shall be an atonement for Me, for that I diminished the moon. And in chapter Elu Treifot, Rabbi Shimon ben Pazi raised a contradiction: it is written (Genesis 1:16) ״ויעש אלהים את שני המאורות הגדולים״ — 'and Elohim made the two great luminaries,' and it is written ״את המאור הגדול ואת המאור הקטן״ — 'the great luminary and the small luminary.' The moon said before the Holy One, blessed be He: Master of the universe! Is it possible for two kings to use one crown? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to her: Go and diminish yourself. She said before Him: Master of the universe! Because I said something fitting before You, I must diminish myself? He said to her: Go and rule by day and by night. She said to Him: What is the greatness — a candle in daylight, what does it profit? He said to her: Go and let Israel count days and years by you. She said to Him: The day too — it is impossible that they not count seasons by it, for it is written (ibid.) ״והיו לאותות ולמועדים ולימים ושנים״. He said to her: Go and let the righteous be called by your name — Ya'akov the Small, Shmuel the Small, David the Small. Her mind was not settled. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: Bring an atonement for Me, for that I diminished the moon. And that is what Reish Lakish said: What is different about the he-goat of Rosh Chodesh, that it is said of it חטאת לה'? The Holy One, blessed be He, said: this he-goat shall be an atonement for Me, for that I diminished the moon. And the explanation of this matter is that the word הגדולים teaches that the sun and the moon were equal in luminosity, and afterward the moon was diminished, and this is why it went back and said (ibid.) ״את המאור הגדול ואת המאור הקטן״. And it was diminished by reason of the accusation that she brought, saying: Is it possible for two kings to use one crown? And she said this for the honor of the Omnipresent, for it would appear that there is no power to make two suns, each with its own light, so that one would not need to receive from the other — and almost the nations would say: from lack of HaShem's power to bestow light upon each and every one. And this accusation was in that she reflected upon the attributes of the Holy One, blessed be He. And after she was diminished and put to shame for her sin, He said to her: Go and rule by day and by night; and further: let Israel count days and years by you; and further: the righteous shall be called by your name. And the Holy One, blessed be He, did all this to soothe her mind, yet she was not appeased until He bestowed honor upon her with the offering of Rosh Chodesh, that they would bring it before Him every time she is renewed. And this is what they said: The Holy One, blessed be He, said — Bring an atonement for Me, for that I diminished the moon. And all this is to teach that the Holy One, blessed be He, does not desire accusation within the work of Creation among His creatures. And further, it is possible that it includes another matter, in order to give an opening to those who repent: from it the lower beings may see and take instruction, that if they return after having sinned, the Holy One, blessed be He, will be appeased with them just as He was appeased with the moon and established atonement-offerings on the day of its renewal. And He also established Rosh HaShanah, which is a day of repentance, on the day of its renewal. And all this is to make known that the Holy One, blessed be He, accepts the repentance of the wicked just as He accepted the moon's and was appeased with her for the sin of accusation. Therefore the righteous are likened to the sun, which had been slighted by the moon, as it is written (Judges 5:31) ״ואוהביו כצאת השמש בגבורתו״. As for the phrase 'for Me' (עלי), the great master Rabbi Yitzchak Alfasi, of blessed memory, wrote in his Halakhot that it is like 'for me' (אלי), and so most of the commentators explained." "<b>And by way of reason (sekhel):</b> לחטאת לה' — 'a sin-offering to HaShem,' and not to the moon. And this he-goat comes to uproot the faith of those who worship the moon, for it was the practice of the nations in ancient days to offer sacrifices to the moon at every new moon. Therefore Scripture needed to specify לה' — 'to HaShem,' meaning to HaShem and not to the moon, so that no one who considers it should think that we offer to the moon and do as the practice of idolaters. And we do not find regarding the other festival he-goats that Scripture mentions חטאת לה' at all, but simply חטאת without specification — since they were eaten and not burned, and therefore it is impossible that it should say of them לה'. And the fact that it is mentioned here with this he-goat, which is also eaten — this was in order to diminish the worship of the moon and to remove that notion from the heart of anyone who harbors doubt about it. This is the approach of the Rambam, of blessed memory." "<b>And on</b> this path the Midrash of the Rabbis, of blessed memory, is to be explained: that the sun and the moon at the beginning of Creation were equal in luminosity — and this is the language of (Genesis 1:16) ״שני המאורות הגדולים״ — for the sun was facing it directly, and one had light by day and the other light by night from the side of the sun that was upon it. And the intention is not that the light of the moon at the beginning of Creation was as great as the light of the sun, but that the two of them were created in their fullness — for all the works of Creation were created in their stature, in their perfection they were created — and this is why it says את שני המאורות הגדולים. And it went back and mentioned המאור הגדול to say that it remained as it was in its greatness. And את המאור הקטן — that it did not remain as it was in its greatness, but was diminished, and so it continues to diminish and wane, unlike the sun, which undergoes neither increase nor decrease. Also, one cannot say that they were equal in the size of their bodies, for the bodies of the sun and the moon at the beginning of Creation were as they are today — this one large and this one small; the body of the moon was not changed or diminished, but only in its luminosity. And the matter of the diminishing of the light is: when the moon saw that it uses the light of the sun and the light was not from itself, it said: Is it possible for two kings to use one crown? And the 'crown' is a metaphor and allegory for the brilliance of the light. And therefore she said: Since I am needed in the lower world just like the sun, to act upon it and govern it, and I am a king like it — why should I not have a crown of my own? For even if my light is not as bright as the light of the sun, at least let it be from myself and not received from another. And she spoke a fitting word. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to her: Go and diminish yourself — that is to say: You suppose that this light that comes to you from the sun in and of itself will always remain so; it shall not be so, but as you proceed you shall diminish. And this is לכי ומעטי את עצמך. She said before Him: Master of the universe! Because I spoke a fitting word before You, I must diminish myself? He said to her: What I created you in this manner, that you receive luminosity from the sun, was out of necessity; but because you spoke a fitting word, My children shall bring an atonement and an offering every time you are renewed." "<b>And the view</b> of Rabbi Shimon, of blessed memory, in this teaching is that they were originally equal in their luminosity in every respect, and the light of the moon was as great as the light of the sun; and afterward the Creator, may He be exalted, diminished it for the benefit of the world and its habitation — for had He not diminished it, the entire time would have been day, and the benefit that comes from night to the lower living beings would have been absent, and its existence nullified, and the world would not have been sustained. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, altered the nature of the moon and reduced its light for the sake of the world's habitation, just as He altered the nature of the waters to gather them all to one place, which is the Ocean. And this is what they said in the Midrash on Kohelet (Ecclesiastes 1:15) ״מעוות לא יוכל לתקון״ — 'that which is crooked cannot be made straight': from the time the waters went astray from the days of Creation and were placed in the Ocean, they were never again set right; from the time the lights went astray in the six days of Creation and the Holy One, blessed be He, diminished the year of the moon from the year of the sun by a certain number of seasons and a certain number of months — they were not set right. Thus far in the Midrash on Kohelet." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: לחטאת לה׳ — 'a sin-offering to YHWH.' The Holy One, blessed be He, said: bring an atonement upon Me, for that I diminished the moon. The sense of 'upon Me' is for what was upon Me: I diminished the moon on My own account and for My sake.'" "<b>And the explanation</b> of the Midrash along this path: the moon said before the Holy One, blessed be He: Master of the universe, is it possible for two kings to use a single crown? He said: 'the Glory is before the Binah' — is it possible for two kings, which are the Tiferet and the Hod, to use a single channel, and that each and every king not have his own channel to receive and draw from above, from before the innermost? The Hod wanted to have its own channel to draw from the Binah like the Tiferet, without needing to draw from the Tiferet. He said to it: go and diminish yourself. This diminution is the cessation of the influx that comes to the Hod from above. The Hod said: because I said something fitting, the influx should be cut off from me? He said to it: go and rule by day and by night. He said to it: Israel shall count days and years by you, and the righteous shall be called by your name — יעקב הקטן, שמואל הקטן — and the explanation of 'by your name,' which is אדני, the lesser. It was not appeased until the Holy One, blessed be He, said that they would offer Him a sacrifice on every New Moon day. And this is what it says: 'the Holy One, blessed be He, said' — that is, the Master of mercy said: bring an atonement for the Hod. And the intention is for what was upon Me, for that I diminished the moon — that is, because the influx of mercy was diminished and cut off from the power of the moon and it returned to judgment, therefore you must bring an atonement in every month at the time of its renewal, in order to draw down to it the influx of mercy from above, and the world shall be uplifted. And this is the secret of זאת עולת חדש בחדשו, for it is the attribute that is uplifted and ascends to receive the influx of mercy. And in the time to come, the sun and the moon shall be equal in light as they were at the beginning, as the word הגדולים indicates, and so shall it be at the end. And this is the word of the prophet, peace be upon him (Isaiah 30:26): והיה אור הלבנה כאור החמה ואור החמה יהיה שבעתים כאור שבעת הימים — that is, after the light of the sun shall be sevenfold. And the reason for this is that the power of the moon, which is the attribute of judgment, shall be unified and uplifted in mercy. And I have already mentioned something of this in the verse (Exodus 15) זה אלי, and this is clear."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:26.489465524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}